>
  <p>Nuvellum publishes reporting, analysis, criticism and cultural writing with an insistence on clarity, provenance and proportion. Each form is named for what it is; each piece is expected to justify the reader’s time.</p>
  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <p>Reporting, analysis, explainers, opinion, reviews and cultural coverage are treated as distinct forms, each with its own obligations. The nature of a piece should never be left for the reader to discover by accident.</p>
  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>Reporting should remain traceable to its sources, serious claims should withstand a higher degree of scrutiny, and material errors should be corrected plainly when they alter what a reader ought to understand.</p>
  <span slot="aside">Beyond the headline is not a promise of length, but of depth. Nuvellum exists for the part of the story that remains after the alert has vanished.</span>
</InstitutionalPage>
